+THE PRIMARY MECHANISM IS NO LONGER IN THIS FILE (DESKTOP-ISOLATION-ENFORCE-1)
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+Everything described below is now DEFENCE IN DEPTH. It is all behavioural --
+env vars the engine may not receive and window geometry it re-asserts on its
+own schedule -- and behavioural mitigation failed the user four times. The
+guarantee now comes from `smoke_lib.isolation`, which moves this process (and
+therefore every child, including the engine, including children of children)
+onto a private Windows WINDOW STATION and DESKTOP that is never passed to
+SwitchDesktop. Measured from inside it: ClipCursor and GetCursorPos return
+ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, OpenDesktop("Default") returns ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND,
+SetCursorPos returns ERROR_REQUIRES_INTERACTIVE_WINDOWSTATION, SendInput
+fails, and a window that explicitly calls ShowWindow(SW_SHOW) still reports
+IsWindowVisible == FALSE and never appears in the user's EnumWindows.
+
+That is the difference in KIND the requirement asked for: an engine build that
+ignores every variable below, calls ShowWindow itself, goes fullscreen and
+calls ClipCursor in a loop STILL cannot touch the user's input space. The env
+vars stay because they cost nothing and they keep the run correct on the rare
+paths isolation cannot cover (see isolation.py's fail-closed contract).
+
+Isolation is established lazily by `apply_env()` / `popen_kwargs()` /
+`spawn()` / `run()` -- i.e. by everything that leads to a launch, including
+the call sites that build their own `subprocess.Popen`. If it cannot be
+established the call RAISES `isolation.IsolationError` and the run aborts.
+There is deliberately no fallback that launches on the user's desktop.
+
 The engine already does the right thing -- but ONLY when it is told to.
